I'd like to suggest the following changes for Patch Level 8 (hope it's
not too late):

1.  Identify traps.
	As is (PL 7) the only way to tell what a trap is after you escaped it
is to go back and possibly activate it again.  This isn't a problem for
pits or bear traps.  But sometimes i'll walk through a rust trap, arrow
trap, dart trap, or squeaky board and miss the message.  I don't want to
go through a rust trap twice.  The '/' command should identify traps (^)
that the player has found in PL 8.

2.  Confirm a swim
	I don't know if anyone else has this problem, but i've lost 2 1/2
characters who accidentally walked into a water-filled area.  The
water-filled area was visible on screen, but i either mis-keyed or
temporarily lost presence of mind, because i walked into the area. (The
1/2 was a character who had an amulet of life-saving, that was used up).
	I can't think of a reason for entering a water-filled area, unless one
is feeling suicidal.  I think Nethack should challenge the player's
intellegence, not his keystroking.  In PL 8, the program should confirm
"really walk into water[y/n]" whenever a character enters a visible
water-filled area.

3.  Repeat command

	As is, the repeat command is okay.  It relieves tedium, and stops
repeating commands when a character is hit.  But it doesn't stop when a
character starts feeling hungry, or if the character is
blind/hallucinating/confused when the blindness/hallucinations/confusion
wears off.  When the character is repeat-searching, the repeats don't
stop when a secret door or trap is found.
	I believe the repeat command should halt whenever the character's
condition changes (to hungry or weak, from confused or blind, etc), or
when a trap/secret door is found, in addition to when a character is
hit.  If i'm repeat-resting after drinking a
blindness/hallucination/confusion potion, i'd like to stop whenever i
can see again/stop hallucinating/don't feel confused.  When i find a
secret door, i'm not going to keep searching.

	The above problems can mostly be avoided by caution/alertness/a little
extra work.  But i believe they shouldn't exists as is, and should be
remedied, if possible, in PL 8.
	
	Btw, i read earlier that scrolls have different effects while the
reader is confused.  The worst of these is the genocide scroll, where
the reader wipes out his own character class, and of course dies.  I
tried this out (accidentally) and not only didn't die, but wiped out an
entire race (in this case, liches).  Either the effects are random, or a
blessed scroll works normally even if the reader is stupid enough to
read it while confused.  In an earlier game, enchant weapon worked as
described with confusion, not granting pluses but making the weapon
rustproof.

